Z||000019||Tigger||10-19-2000||10:37 AM||||I think what we are seeing is pretty much what would be expected.  Great idea, cool concept, poor execution... the Aztek is a recent example.<P>I definitely agree that those "production" 89 Fiero's sitting in the back lot are very different from the pictures of the concept '89s shown in magazines.  Kind of watered down, and almost look like the panels would fit under the subframe of our cars.<P>When I first saw the concept renderings of the Pontiac Pirahna last year I though maybe Pontiac was trying to look into a cool looking sports car, but after seeing the real concept car, it looks blah, I'd hate to see what it would look like as a production car.  One great feature of the Piranha... you can use a garden hose to hose out the interior, oookay.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
